/* book exam traps: K is not a fixed percentage or a tuned constant. It is recomputed from P and R at every step; writing 'K = 0.5 always' is the classic mistake. | The innovation is measurement minus prediction, z − H x. Reversing it pushes the estimate away from the fix instead of towards it. | Q and R are swapped under exam pressure. Q is process noise (how much the INS model is distrusted); R is measurement noise (the GPS error budget). | P grows during predict and shrinks during update. Forgetting the growth makes the filter overconfident and it stops listening to GPS. */
